ProsperoSunshine: the stream's UDP ports open at the first RTSP SETUP instead of at ANNOUNCE

Moonlight starts its audio ping as soon as the SETUP for audio is answered (moonlight-common-c, AudioStream.c, for GameStream's
sake), but Sunshine opened its UDP ports only at ANNOUNCE, a few round trips later. The first ping went to a closed port, and
the console answers that with ICMP port unreachable (measured with no stream running: a connected socket gets ECONNREFUSED
on 48000 and 47998). A direct client doesn't care. ps5-tailscale relays each client over a connected UDP socket to
127.0.0.1, and its reply loop ends on that error while the pings keep the flow alive: the host's audio then never reaches
the client (issue 37: picture, no sound, over Tailscale only; reported upstream as holdmysocks/ps5-tailscale#10).

stream::hold_ports() takes a reference on the broadcast context, which opens the ports, and the launch session keeps it
from its first SETUP until ANNOUNCE has started the session (which holds its own) or failed. A launch session that never
gets to ANNOUNCE drops it with the launch session.

--- a/src/rtsp.cpp
+++ b/src/rtsp.cpp
@@ -1046,6 +1046,12 @@
       return;
     }
 
+    // ProsperoSunshine: open the ports before the client learns them; its audio pings start with this answer.
+    if (!session.held_ports) {
+      session.held_ports = stream::hold_ports();
+      BOOST_LOG(debug) << "Stream ports "sv << (session.held_ports ? "open from SETUP"sv : "could not be opened at SETUP"sv);
+    }
+
     seqn.next = &session_option;
 
     session_option.option = const_cast<char *>("Session");
@@ -1316,7 +1322,10 @@
     auto stream_session = stream::session::alloc(config, session);
     rtsp_server->insert(stream_session);
 
-    if (stream::session::start(*stream_session, sock.remote_endpoint().address().to_string())) {
+    const bool started = stream::session::start(*stream_session, sock.remote_endpoint().address().to_string()) == 0;
+    // ProsperoSunshine: the session holds the ports now, or the start failed; the hold from SETUP is no longer needed.
+    session.held_ports.reset();
+    if (!started) {
       BOOST_LOG(error) << "Failed to start a streaming session"sv;
 
       rtsp_server->remove(stream_session);
